Description: build: use the bundled fmt unless WITH_SYSTEM_FMT is set
 Reef builds against the system fmt whenever it is new enough. fmt 10 and
 later (Debian trixie and forky) no longer format types like ceph_le<>
 implicitly, so e.g. src/msg/async/frames_v2.cc fails with "Cannot format
 an argument". Squid uses its bundled fmt by default and the system one
 only with WITH_SYSTEM_FMT (upstream 421bf61fee35 and follow-ups); do the
 same for reef. The bundled fmt is 9.1.
---
--- a/src/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/src/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -325,3 +325,8 @@
   STRING "build with fmt version")
-find_package(fmt ${WITH_FMT_VERSION} QUIET)
+# Like squid: use the bundled fmt unless the system one is asked for; fmt 10
+# and later (Debian trixie, forky) cannot format ceph_le<> and friends.
+option(WITH_SYSTEM_FMT "build against system fmt" OFF)
+if(WITH_SYSTEM_FMT)
+  find_package(fmt ${WITH_FMT_VERSION} QUIET)
+endif()
 if(fmt_FOUND)
